# What NOT to upload to Vercel.
#
# This matters for more than build size. With no framework detected, Vercel
# treats the output directory as a static site — so anything left here can be
# fetched from the deployment URL. `vercel.json` points the output directory at
# an empty `public/`, and this file is the second layer: the screenshots and the
# retired pipeline never reach the deployment at all.
#
# Do NOT add tracker/, holdings.json, api/, requirements.txt or vercel.json —
# the function needs them.

# Real banking screenshots. Never deploy these.
screenshots/

# Tests and local tooling
tests/
pytest.ini
test_parse.py
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
__pycache__/
logs/

# Retired Telegram pipeline — kept in the repo for rollback, unused at runtime
bot.py
render.py
portfolio_tracker.py
requirements-bot.txt
Procfile

# Source for the Apps Script side, deployed separately inside Google
portfolio_gas.js

# Docs — read on GitHub, not served
*.md
